|#E8EAF6|MQ / HTTP Trigger|
|#FFF3E0|Parent Handler|
|#ECF6EF|Worker Goroutines|

start

|MQ / HTTP Trigger|
:Message received from one of the queues;
note right
  6 Main Queues -> 6 Main Processes:
  1) jobs.ticks.regular     -> Ticks Regular        (every hour, minute :05)
  2) jobs.ticks.backfill    -> Backfill Ticks       (every 10 minutes)
  3) jobs.candles.regular   -> Candles Regular      (seed 00:00 UTC, aggregate 05:08 UTC)
  4) jobs.candles.backfill  -> Backfill Candles     (every 20 minutes, from minute :04)
  5) jobs.maintenance       -> Maintenance          (every 5 minutes, from minute :02)
  6) jobs.sync              -> Sync (Outbox Worker) (every 5 minutes)

  See the detailed flow of each process in:
   01-ticks-regular.puml
   02-backfill-ticks.puml
   03-candles-regular.puml
   04-backfill-candles.puml
   05-maintenance.puml
   06-sync-outbox.puml
end note

switch (Which queue triggered it?)
case ( jobs.ticks.regular / jobs.ticks.backfill )
  :RunTickParentHandler(mode);<<handler>>
  note right: mode = REGULAR or BACKFILL
case ( jobs.candles.regular / jobs.candles.backfill )
  :RunCandleParentHandler(mode);<<handler>>
  note right: mode = REGULAR or BACKFILL
case ( jobs.maintenance )
  :RunMaintenanceHandler();<<handler>>
case ( jobs.sync )
  :RunSyncHandler();<<handler>>
endswitch

|Parent Handler|
:onStarted() — record activity log entry immediately;<<db>>
note right
  Every trigger is logged at the start.
  No trigger is silently dropped or discarded.
end note

:Fork child goroutines (wg.Add + go func), each carrying ctx & DAL;
note right
  REGULAR mode forks 3 goroutines: T-0, T-1, T-2
  BACKFILL mode forks 1 goroutine:  Master Bulk-Claim (up to 120 rows,
                                    routed in-memory to Ingestion/Reset/Validation)
  MAINTENANCE forks 4 goroutines:   A (Forward Seeding), B (Backward Gap Fill),
                                    C (Pruning), D (Consistency Check)

  Concurrency is managed entirely by PostgreSQL transactions:
  every DB operation uses dal.Execute(ctx, fn) → a single PostgreSQL
  transaction. Row-level mutual exclusion is enforced by
  FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED inside each claim query.

  Each goroutine MUST register:
    defer recoverGoroutine(ctx, "name")   — panic safety
    defer wg.Done()                       — Fork-Join guarantee
end note

:wg.Wait() — block until all goroutines finish (Fork-Join);

|Parent Handler|
stop

@enduml
